{title: The Long Road Home}
{artist: Sample song}
{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Morning light is [G]falling on the [Am]road
[F]Every step is [C]bringing us back [G]home
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Carry on, [C]carry on
[G]We can hear the [Am]morning song
{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]When the night is [G]quiet we will [Am]know
[F]All the roads we [C]travel lead us [G]home
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Carry on, [C]carry on
[G]We can hear the [Am]morning song
{end_of_chorus}
{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Past the station, [G]down beside the [Am]stream
[F]Through the valley, [C]where the lanterns [G]gleam
[C]Take the footpath [G]round the maple [Am]tree
[F]Leave the gate wide [C]open there for [G]me
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Hear the river [G]underneath the [Am]bridge
[F]See the rainclouds [C]moving past the [G]ridge
[C]When the evening [G]settles on the [Am]field
[F]We will follow [C]where the road is [G]sealed
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[C]One more mile and [G]then the road will [Am]bend
[F]We can see the [C]village at the [G]end
[C]There the lights will [G]guide us through the [Am]rain
[F]To the place we'll [C]call our home a[G]gain
{end_of_verse}
